1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:07,200
I don't think hell exists. I happen to believe in life after death, but I don't think it's got a thing to do with reward and punishment.

2
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:13,760
Religion is always in the control business, and that's something people don't really understand.

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:17,540
It's in the guilt-producing, control business.

4
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:24,940
And if you have heaven as a place where you're rewarded for your goodness and hell as a place where you're punished for your evil,

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,860
then you sort of have control of the population.

6
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:36,080
And so they create this fiery place, which has quite literally scared the hell out of a lot of people throughout Christian history.

7
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:38,440
And it's part of a control tactic.

8
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:44,780
But wait a minute, you're saying that hell, the idea of a place under the earth or somewhere where you're tormented for an eternity,

9
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:47,240
is actually an invention of the church?

10
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:50,360
I think the church fired its furnaces hotter than anybody else.

11
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:56,560
But I think there's a sense in most religious life of reward and punishment in some form.

12
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:01,520
The church doesn't like for people to grow up because you can't control grown-ups.

13
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,900
That's why we talk about being born again.

14
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,760
When you're born again, you're still a child.

15
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,740
The people don't need to be born again.

16
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:09,580
They need to grow up.

17
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:12,620
They need to accept their responsibility for themselves and the world.

18
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:18,660
What do you make of the theology, which is quite prominent these days in America,

19
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:26,040
which is that there is one guaranteed way not to go to hell, and that is to accept Jesus as your personal Savior.

20
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,880
Yeah, I grew up in that tradition.

21
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:34,380
Every church I know claims that we are the true church, and they have some ultimate authority.

22
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:35,820
We have the infallible Pope.

23
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:37,200
We have the inerrant Bible.

24
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:44,840
The idea that the truth of God can be bound in any human system, by any human creed, by any human book,

25
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,960
is almost beyond imagination for me.

26
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:50,600
I mean, God is not a Christian.

27
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:54,180
God is not a Jew or a Muslim or a Hindu or a Buddhist.

28
00:01:54,180 --> 00:02:01,460
All of those are human systems, which human beings have created to try to help us walk into the mystery of God.

29
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:02,820
I honor my tradition.

30
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:05,000
I walk through my tradition.

31
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:08,240
But I don't believe my tradition defines God.

32
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,220
Life is a startling and wondrous experience.

33
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:20,100
And eventually, I think we're going to discover that God is unfolding through the life of our consciousness and our self-consciousness

34
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:22,560
and is not a parent figure up in the sky.

35
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:26,880
But I believe because I'm related to something that is not bound by time and space,

36
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,700
that I will share in whatever God's eternity is.

